below.

These files (the traced outline, the generated SVGs, and the page and script in
this folder) carry the LLM-Rosetta mark and belong to the project. The source
code of the project is MIT licensed; that license does not cover these files.

You may:

- use the mark to refer to the LLM-Rosetta project, in articles, tutorials,
  talks, documentation, package listings and screenshots;
- copy and redistribute these files unchanged, with this notice, as part of a
  fork or a mirror of this repository;
- use the mark in a non-commercial project built on LLM-Rosetta, with a visible
  note that the project is not the official LLM-Rosetta.

You may not:

- use this mark, or a confusingly similar one, as the logo, icon or name of
  your own product, company, service or hosted offering;
- use it in a commercial product, service or marketing, or in any way that
  suggests endorsement by Peng Ding or the LLM-Rosetta maintainers;
- claim authorship or ownership of the mark, register it as a trademark, or
  register a confusingly similar one;
- redistribute a modified version of the mark without saying that it is
  modified.

The outline was traced from File:Rosetta Stone.svg on Wikimedia Commons, which
its author released under CC0 1.0 (recorded in references/SOURCE.md). CC0
covers that source image, not these files. What these terms protect is the
specific simplified geometry, framing and files, not the shape of an ancient
stone.

For permission, open an issue in https://github.com/Oaklight/llm-rosetta.
